---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Heading from '../Heading.astro';

const reasons = [
  {
    title: 'The same inputs produce the same output.',
    body: 'That makes a diff useful for review and lets Kix reproduce a previous deployment.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Values carry their references with them.',
    body: 'When an app reads a database address, Kix can follow that value back to the database resource and include the dependency in its plan.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The whole definition is evaluated first.',
    body: 'Kix can run its checks against the complete definition before it applies anything.',
  },
  { title: 'Reading a definition changes nothing.', body: 'Reading a definition leaves the cluster unchanged.' },
  {
    title: 'Built on an established language.',
    body: 'Nix has described reproducible operating systems for two decades. Kix uses that existing language.',
  },
];
---

<Section tone="paper-2" labelledby="language-title">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-12 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-end gap-10 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_480px] xl:gap-20">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
        <Heading id="language-title">Why the Nix language?</Heading>
        <p class="text-[17px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2 md:text-[18px]">
          Kix definitions use the Nix language. Its evaluation model lets Kix read the complete cluster before
          deployment and retain the references between values, which are the basis for the checks and plan shown above.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 rounded-[10px] border-[1.5px] border-ink bg-paper p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-[13px] text-accent-text">the syntax may be unfamiliar</p>
        <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-[1.55] text-ink">
          The syntax may take some getting used to. You can start with an existing definition, make a small change, and
          use Kix's errors to see how it affects the cluster.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-5">
      {
        reasons.map((reason) => (
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-t-[1.5px] border-ink pt-5">
            <h3 class="text-[18px] leading-[1.3] font-semibold">{reason.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-[14.5px] leading-[1.55] text-ink-2">{reason.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</Section>
